// src/v4/extdeps/languages/resolver.dag
//
// Scope: the SHARED registry for D2-resolver types — types used by every
//        extdeps/languages/* file that are STRUCTURALLY LANGUAGE-INVARIANT
//        (their structure provably cannot vary across the modeled language
//        specs). These are convergence carriers: one declaration, imported
//        by each language file, never re-declared.
// Anchor: src/v4/DECISIONS.md row D4 (operator-ratified 2026-05-16) — the
//         governing decision that homes the shared resolver types here.
//         D4 completes D2 (the extdeps resolver shape): D2 specified the
//         per-primitive three-thin-facts shape; D4 pins WHERE D2's shared
//         types live so the five language files import rather than
//         re-declare (parallel-declaration P2 forbids).
//
// Admission rule (STRICT — per D4):
//   resolver.dag hosts ONLY structurally-language-INVARIANT resolver
//   types. The admission test is a proof obligation: can you prove the
//   type's structure is invariant across the modeled language specs?
//   - GroundingMap<IRCarrier> { spelling: String } PASSES — every modeled
//     language grounds an IR carrier to exactly one surface spelling
//     string; the record shape does not vary.
//   - Spec-VARYING types STAY per-language and are NOT admitted here:
//     OverflowDisposition (Rust panic-or-wrap vs Go wrap vs C/C++ UB vs
//     Python arbitrary-precision — the variant set itself varies),
//     NaN/Inf handling carriers, language-grammar facts. Those are D2.5 /
//     L-2 per-language facts; homing them here would re-import the
//     parallel-taxonomy anti-pattern this file exists to prevent.
//   Future structurally-invariant shared resolver types (e.g. a
//   C5-fidelity Modeled | Declared-normalized | Fail-closed disposition
//   classifier) land here without a fresh placement decision — D4 is the
//   standing ratification for this file's purpose.
//
// Owns:
//   - GroundingMap<IRCarrier> { spelling: String } — the per-primitive
//     surface-spelling carrier (D2's D2a(2) "grounding map"). IRCarrier is
//     a phantom type parameter naming the IR carrier this grounding maps
//     (RustI32, PyInt, GoInt64, ...); each language file declares
//     per-primitive instances `data <lang>_<prim>_grounding:
//     GroundingMap<<AliasCarrier>> = GroundingMap { spelling: "<token>" }`.
//     `spelling` is a String boundary value — the canonical source text
//     for emit / ingest, living at the source-syntax boundary, not in
//     kernel/lens code.
//
// Consumes:
//   - (none) — String is kernel-ambient (STRUCTURE.md:147-148); no import
//     is required. resolver.dag is a zero-import leaf of the .dag tree.
//
// Status: T-4 D4 — file created 2026-05-17 (keen-gull-671), the
//   encoding-half of operator-ratified D4 (DECISIONS.md, PR #3216).
//   Created in parallel with #3216; lands after #3216 merges the D4/D5
//   rows to main. The per-language `import … resolver { GroundingMap }`
//   lines + per-primitive `data <lang>_<prim>_grounding` instances are a
//   separate fan-out (canonical rust.dag first, then python/go/cpp/ts) —
//   NOT this file's scope. rust.dag's current provisional GroundingMap
//   declaration (the 🟡 TRACKED-SCAFFOLD at rust.dag:1718) relocates here
//   in that fan-out; this file is its pinned home.
//
// Closed-tree extension (per D4 + INVARIANTS #1): this file is a
//   ratified addition to the closed .dag tree. STRUCTURE.md's enumeration
//   gains the resolver.dag line; the checksum count is bumped to match.
//   The enumeration — not the count — is authoritative.
//
// Brief: this file's I/O contract is the immutable contract for the
//   worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator ratification
//   (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.extdeps.languages.resolver


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// GroundingMap<IRCarrier> — the per-primitive surface-spelling carrier.
//
// A Conj record (no Practice-4 ledger — a single-field product, not an
// enumeration). IRCarrier is a phantom type parameter: it does not appear
// in the body; it names — at the type level — which IR carrier a given
// grounding instance maps, so `GroundingMap<RustI32>` and
// `GroundingMap<PyInt>` are distinct facts (P1/P2 fidelity).
//
// The structure is provably language-INVARIANT: every modeled language
// spec grounds each IR carrier to exactly one canonical surface spelling.
// What VARIES across languages is the spelling VALUE (`i32` vs `int` vs
// `int64`) — carried by per-language `data` instances — never the record
// SHAPE. This is exactly the D4 admission test, and is why GroundingMap
// is the first resident here rather than re-declared five times.
type GroundingMap<IRCarrier> {
  spelling: String
}
